Until document is completed, use '\qtwopages \shipout\vbox{}' instead of '\quire{...}'

=======================================================================================
DESIGN DECISIONS:

MakePK generates pk files for ./ fonts on each run, because mf mode may be different on each run
(this automatically covers the case when pk file did not exist previously).
Also, if you are editing a character, you want to see new version of it on each run,
even though the same mode was used for generating previous pk file with this character.

We need to use different files (both having 'ps' extension) for printing and for viewing
because we do not want a file with one and the same name to contain content generated for different
metafont modes.
File for viewer is created in working directory, with the same name as source document.
File created for printing is /tmp/PRINT.ps - we can use one file name for all documents
because the file is used immediately after being written.

Default \pdfhorigin and \pdfvorigin for letter paper are 1in; to use default \hsize and \vsize for
a4 paper they are changed as follows:
  (210-6.5*25.4)/2=22.45mm
  (297-9*25.4)/2=34.2mm

Start mf file with %! line if you need to set geometry, for example:
  %! pdfpagewidth=210mm pdfpageheight=297mm pdfhorigin=4.1mm pdfvorigin=20mm

\pdfpagewidth, \pdfpageheight, \pdfhorigin and \pdfvorigin are stored in comment of dvi file
and are subsequently used as arguments to dvips.

Use \pdfhorigin and \pdfvorigin to set margins (this is not the role of \hoffset and \voffset).
